  "script": "The Corvette Z06 3LZ screams performance from the get-go. Check out the aggressive front air intake and hood vent, crafted to optimize airflow and cooling for this beastly machine. Along the side, the prominent Z06 badge is not just an aesthetic detail; it\u2019s a declaration of intent, highlighting its legendary high-performance pedigree. Under the hood, the 2011 Corvette Z06 is powered by a monstrous 7.0-liter LS7 V8, delivering 505 horsepower and 470 lb-ft of torque. This engine is all about raw power and engineering finesse. Inside, the six-speed manual gearbox ensures a pure driving experience. The metal shifter feels robust and direct, making every shift a thrill for true driving enthusiasts. At the rear, the quad exhaust setup is more than eye candy. It allows the Z06 to breathe better and roar louder, announcing its presence even at a distance. Originally priced around $75K, the Z06 now trades for about $45K, with a depreciation rate of roughly 8% per year. This makes it a compelling value for performance seekers.",
